/	REVISED DECEMBER 4, 1972
/
/
/	ABSTRACT
/	--------
/	UTIL2.SB IS THE MODIFIED VERSION OF THE PS/8 FORTRAN II
/	LIBRARY PROGRAM UTILTY.SB. THERE ARE CHANGES IN SOME OF
/	THE I/O DEVICES TO ALLOW THE USE OF A PT08 OR DC02G AS DEVICE
/	2 (AS A TELETYPE), AN A.B. DICK 960 VIDEOJET AS DEVICE 3, AND
/	A NON-ECHO PT08/DCO2G AS DEVICE 3 INPUT. CONTROL/Z ON DEVICE
/	4 INPUT CAN BE DETECTED BY A NEW SUBROUTINE "EOF". UTIL2.SB
/	MAY BE CONDITIONALLY ASSEMBLED WITH SABR AS A PT08 OR DC02G OR 
/	A.B. DICK 960 VIDEOJET SUBROUTINE. UTIL28.RL IS A VERSION FOR
/	PT08 AND A.B. DICK VIDEOJET. UTIL2G.RL IS A VERSION FOR DC02G.
/
/
/
/**PAGE
/INTRODUCTION
/------------
/UTIL2.SB  IS THE MODIFIED VERSION OF UTILTY.SB FOR THE PS/8 FORTRAN 
/LIBRARY CURRENTLY IN THE LIB8.RL FILE. IT  REPLACES THE DEC LPT: WITH
/A HANDLER FOR THE AB DICK 960 LINEPRINTER WITH ECLECTIC COMPUTER CORP-
/ORATION INTERFACE. A DCO2G SERIAL INTERFACE MAY BE USED IN PLACE OF
/THE LINEPRINTER. THE CARD READ (DEVICE 3 FOR  INPUT) IS  REPLACED
/WITH  A PT08 (OR DC02G) INPUT HANDLER WHICH DOES NOT ECHO INPUT.
/DEVICE 2 WHICH  WAS THE  HI-SPEED PAPER TAPE READER IS NOW A
/PT08 (OR DCO2G) INPUT/OUTPUT DEVICE WITH ECHO (SO THE PT08 (OR DCO2G)
/LOOKS LIKE A TELETYPE..)..
/
/
/
/END OF FILE DETECTION
/---------------------
/THE GENERAL  DEVICE # 4 ON  INPUT, SETS AN  END OF FILE
/FLAG (IEOF) TO -1 ON  SEEING A ^Z. IT IS NORMALLY  SET TO 0.
/THE USER MUST  INITIALLY SET THE FLAG TO 0, AND THEN HE  MAY
/TEST IT AT ANY TIME BY DOING A "CALL EOF(IFLAG)". IFLAG WILL THEN BE
/SET TO -1 OR 0. EVERYTIME  SUBROUTINE EOF(IFLAG) IS CALLED
/IT SETS IFLAG TO THE CURRENT VALUE OF  IEOF AND  THEN SETS IEOF
/TO ZERO. THIS  IS HOW  IT IS INITIALLY CLEARED (I.E. BY CALLING IT
/AND IGNORING THE VALUE OF IFLAG THE FIRST TIME IT IS CALLED.).
/THIS IS SUMMARIZED BELOW:
/	IFLAG	MEANING
/	-----	-------
/	0	CONTROL/Z (EOF) NOT SEEN YET.
/	-1	CONTROL/Z (EOF) WAS DETECTED SINCE SUBR EOF WAS LAST
/		CALLED.
/
/
/OTHER CHANGES
/-------------
/TWO OTHER CHANGES MADE TO UTILTY.SB ARE THAT THE "OPEN" SUBROUTINE
/DOES NOT DO A LINE FEED. RATHER, IT SENDS A NULL OR "000" AND THE
/CONTROL/C TRAP IN THE TELETYPE ROUTINE IS REMOVED.
/
/
/
/
/CONDITIONAL ASSEMBLY 
/--------------------
/UTIL2.SB MAY BE CONFIGURED FOR A PT08 OR A DCO2G. IF IT IS
/FOR A PT08, THEN REMOVE THE / IN
/	ABSYM PT08 1
/IF IT IS FOR A DC02G, THEN GROUP 0 STATION 1 IS DEVICE #2
/AND GROUP 0 STATION 2 IS DEVICE #3. REMOVE THE / IN
/	ABSYM DC02 1
/IF THE AB DICK LINEPRINTER IS DEFINED RATHER THAN THE DC02G THEN
/REMOVE THE / IN
/	ABSYM ABDICK 1
/
/
/
/
/
/
/THE CURRENT DEVICES ARE:
/DEVICE #       INPUT          OUTPUT
/-------------------------------------
/  1	   TTY WITH ECHO	TTY
/  2	   PT08 WITH ECHO	PT08 (OR DCO2G STATION 1, GROUP 0)
/  3	   PT08  NO ECHO	LPT: (OR DCO2G STATION 2, GROUP 0)
/  4	   GENERAL		GENERAL  (EOF TRAP IS ACTIVE)
/
/USING UTIL2
/-----------
/TO USE UTIL2.SB, IT MUST BE  ASSEMBLED UNDER  SABER THEN
/LOADED BEFORE !!! THE LIB8.RL/L HAS  BEEN LOADED.
/EG.
/	.R SABR
/	*UTIL2.RL,UTIL2.LS_UTIL2.SB
/	.R LOADER	/CALL  THE  RELOC. LOADER.
/	*MAIN.RL	/LOAD THE MAIN
/	*UTIL2.RL$	/OVERLAY THE  NEW UTILITY  PACKAGE.
/	*LIB8.RL/L	/LOAD THE  LIBRARY ROUTINES.
/	.SAVE DSK:MAIN  /SAVE  IT
/
/       COPYRIGHT 1968, DIGITAL EQUIPMENT CORP., MAYNARD, MASS.
/       UTILITY SUBROUTINE PACKAGE
/               VERSION UTILTY.V07 (JANUARY 7, 1969)
